    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Christian Yelich**, who paces the squad with a 75.84 efficiency score. His favorable matchup against Lowder provides the day\u2019s most significant platoon edge, compounded by his leadoff spot and a strong projection profile. Joining him in the top tier is **Trea Turner** (69.58) and **Kyle Schwarber** (67.42). While **Trea Turner** faces a modest tax for the opposing catcher\u2019s quick pop-time, his leadoff placement and speed profile remain essential for our stolen base targets. **Kyle Schwarber** continues to be a staple in our lineup, and even with the defensive and platoon adjustments, his xwOBA of .394 creates a high floor against Chandler.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involves **Colt Keith**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a 47.16 score. While he remains a potent asset, the optimizer prioritized the high-efficiency matchup of **Chase Meidroth** (61.95), who benefits significantly from a favorable park factor and a weak matchup against Gibson. Furthermore, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (63.81) makes the lineup despite a challenging platoon split against Sears, as his elite sprint speed is vital to our scarcity-driven strategy, even when facing a tough left-handed arm. **Yordan Alvarez** remains a start at 55.77; while his SP_xERA matchup against Ryan is the toughest among our starters, his elite .443 xwOBA ensures he maintains value regardless of the opposing skill level.\n\nManagement must remain vigilant regarding the risks inherent in today's matchups. While **Junior Caminero** (64.45) is a locked-in play, the lack of lineup confirmation for some games introduces minor volatility. We are currently navigating a \"below floor\" scenario with **Dillon Dingler**, who remains benched with a 36.99 score, failing to overcome his negative platoon profile against the current opposing pitcher. We continue to monitor the status of **Hyeseong Kim**, who remains unavailable in the minors. As always, our commitment to speed-first acquisition means we are keeping a close eye on **Zac Veen**, **Rece Hinds**, and **Josh Smith** should any mid-game pinch-hit opportunities arise to bolster our stolen base totals.",
